Files: library-boundary.vine; Cargo.toml; crates/**; tests/**; evidence/**; index.md; proposals/**
Do: Build one ownership table for every workspace crate, executable, test workspace, evidence artifact, and design record. Classify each as temporal library, host library, Caravan reference implementation, sample application, target adapter, evidence, or planning/tooling. Record production dependencies separately from dev-dependencies and identify each current Caravan or target edge crossing a proposed library boundary.
Accept: Every named component has exactly one owner class and one owning contract; each current production contamination is named with its source and destination; test-only reference usage is distinguished from public dependency contamination; and no remediation task relies on an unrecorded classification.
