[core-contract] Settle the reusable temporal library contract (complete)
Files: proposals/library-contract.md; crates/engine-time/**; crates/engine-sdk/**; crates/engine-journal/**; crates/engine-branches/**; crates/engine-index/**; crates/engine-presentation/**
Do: Specify the smallest reusable temporal library surface from concrete external-consumer needs. Name the public types and functions for fixed-point time, immutable context and journal values, journal-owned timestamp authoring, direct indexed state queries, immutable branch creation, lookahead, persistence, and state-plus-Tau presentation. Define ownership, visibility, error behavior, payload parameterization, Send/static requirements where applicable, and the boundary between generic mechanics and game-owned rules without silently preserving Caravan-shaped APIs.
Accept: The contract contains no Caravan or platform identifiers; Worldline + LogicalTime -> GameState is directly queryable and query-order independent; JournalWriter remains the timestamp authority; actual/counterfactual/corrected branches remain immutable values; persistence carries library-approved values rather than frames or host state; GameState + Tau is the only render-production input; unresolved choices are recorded as decisions; and an external-style consumer can be designed without importing implementation modules.
-> classification
@artifact text/markdown proposals/library-contract.md
