[reference-contract] Delineate the Caravan reference implementation and sample game (complete)
Files: proposals/library-contract.md; crates/caravan-domain/**; crates/caravan-vegetation/**; crates/caravan-hazards/**; crates/caravan-seeded/**; crates/caravan-reference/**; crates/caravan-demo/**; tests/conformance/**
Do: Assign Caravan geometry, journal vocabulary, indexed rules, seeded fixtures, reference projection, orchestration, and terminal/demo presentation to the reference-game or sample-consumer boundary. State which public library contracts the reference implementation exercises and which behavior is evidence only. Keep the anchor semantics authoritative for the reference world without presenting its types or rule order as generic engine primitives.
Accept: Caravan-specific values and rules have one owner outside the generic library; caravan-reference is explicitly a reference oracle/client; caravan-demo is explicitly a removable sample consumer; conformance cases identify whether they test public library behavior or reference-game behavior; and no sample convenience API is required by the library contract.
