Do: Settle nworlds-host as an adjacent reusable host boundary rather than an application-owned game loop. Define GamePackage, InputIngress, RenderSink, StorageTransport, and platform translation responsibilities, including ownership and error flow. Separate passive transport/execution from game meaning, authoritative time, persistence semantics, and target resolution; classify ApplicationHost as a convenience composition only if the contract requires it.
Accept: nworlds-host builds with no Caravan, target, window, or backend dependency; host ports transport already-owned values; the package owns semantic control order and immutable publication; no host clock or device handle enters GameState or render production; target-specific composition remains a consumer; and any retained convenience host API has an external-consumer reason.
